Correct collapsed blur bounds and reject unsupported float32 normalization domains.

MilkDrop3 code/vis_milk2/milkdropfs.cpp GetSafeBlurMinMax contains the same
avg-minus typo. Correct the documented push-apart intent at all three levels;
retain its clamp-then-expand ordering and ordinary float32 coefficient arithmetic.
This is a safety correction, not a backport of an already-fixed reference.

Reject nonfinite or out-of-float32 equation inputs. If adjustment overflows,
0.1 cannot be represented around its midpoint, or progressive float32 coordinates
or shader coefficients are nonfinite/zero, use coherent [0,1] bounds at all levels.
Representable ordinary and extreme ranges retain their bounds and coefficients.
GetSafeBlurMinMaxValues and Update share the actual coefficient producer.

